[2026-03-14T22:48:35.762Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CxKktLjzeV4nan3T6586v6","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Skill Reference\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It supports recording, uploading, and managing recordings with authentication via API key.\n\n## Installation\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\nGenerate an API key from https://app.replay.io settings and set it as the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and capture a session |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Send recordings to the cloud |\n| `list` | View all local recordings with details |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete recordings locally |\n| `login`/`logout` | Manage account authentication |\n| `info` | Check installed versions |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Upload source maps for debugging |\n\n## Common Workflow\n\n1. **Record**: `replayio record https://yourapp.com`\n2. **Upload**: `replayio upload <recording-id>` (or use interactive menu without arguments)\n3. **Debug**: Access the recorded session via the returned URL\n\nThe tool automatically checks for updates and can be configured with Claude's MCP server for integrated debugging capabilities."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f4e5d6b-4fb9-41f9-a901-1702b878282d","uuid":"c675e65f-1472-4aab-bbd1-cebde615376a","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Skill Reference\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It supports recording, uploading, and managing recordings with authentication via API key.\n\n## Installation\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\nGenerate an API key from https://app.replay.io settings and set it as the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and capture a session |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Send recordings to the cloud |\n| `list` | View all local recordings with details |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete recordings locally |\n| `login`/`logout` | Manage account authentication |\n| `info` | Check installed versions |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Upload source maps for debugging |\n\n## Common Workflow\n\n1. **Record**: `replayio record https://yourapp.com`\n2. **Upload**: `replayio upload <recording-id>` (or use interactive menu without arguments)\n3. **Debug**: Access the recorded session via the returned URL\n\nThe tool automatically checks for updates and can be configured with Claude's MCP server for integrated debugging capabilities.","durationMs":3720,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-14T22:48:36.688Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0147i88sScwjDB9CF3jQVC7C","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\n**Name:** replay-mcp\n\n**Description:** Tool for inspecting https://replay.io recordings to investigate web app behavior.\n\n**Key Capabilities:**\n\nThe tool provides three main categories of functionality:\n\n1. **Exploratory Tools** - Discover what happened in recordings:\n   - Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n   - Timeline analysis (console messages, storage access, network requests, React renders)\n   - Source code inspection (find, read, and search JavaScript files with execution hit counts)\n\n2. **Explanatory Tools** - Understand why events occurred:\n   - Dependencies tracking (call stacks, control flow analysis)\n   - State details (point descriptions, element inspection, React component trees, expression evaluation)\n\n3. **Investigation Methodology** - Recommended approach includes:\n   - Framing specific questions about app behavior\n   - Using exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n   - Applying explanatory tools to understand causation\n   - Forming evidence-based hypotheses\n   - Supporting conclusions with gathered data\n\nThe recordings function as \"a gigantic database\" capturing complete execution history, with \"points\" marking individual statement executions and \"elements\" representing DOM references throughout their lifetime."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f4e5d6b-4fb9-41f9-a901-1702b878282d","uuid":"5c54ae25-4fdc-4050-8b60-484eccf9273c","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\n**Name:** replay-mcp\n\n**Description:** Tool for inspecting https://replay.io recordings to investigate web app behavior.\n\n**Key Capabilities:**\n\nThe tool provides three main categories of functionality:\n\n1. **Exploratory Tools** - Discover what happened in recordings:\n   - Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n   - Timeline analysis (console messages, storage access, network requests, React renders)\n   - Source code inspection (find, read, and search JavaScript files with execution hit counts)\n\n2. **Explanatory Tools** - Understand why events occurred:\n   - Dependencies tracking (call stacks, control flow analysis)\n   - State details (point descriptions, element inspection, React component trees, expression evaluation)\n\n3. **Investigation Methodology** - Recommended approach includes:\n   - Framing specific questions about app behavior\n   - Using exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n   - Applying explanatory tools to understand causation\n   - Forming evidence-based hypotheses\n   - Supporting conclusions with gathered data\n\nThe recordings function as \"a gigantic database\" capturing complete execution history, with \"points\" marking individual statement executions and \"elements\" representing DOM references throughout their lifetime.","durationMs":3414,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
